Modifications by TechnoWolfTV (2025-2026)

The following changes were made to the original weather_pack mod by
Artūras Norkus (xeranas) and are released under the same MIT License above.

-- Administrative / housekeeping changes --

- Removed deprecated files: depends.txt, description.txt
- mod.conf: Updated to modern format with the following content:
    name = weather_pack
    description = Set of weathers for minetest
    optional_depends = lightning

-- Weather frequency rebalancing --

All weather types reduced to approximately 25% of their original spawn
frequency to better suit long-play sessions:

- heavy_rain: local heavy_rain_chance = 0.015 (tropical: 0.1)
- light_rain:  chance = 0.0375
- rain:        chance = 0.025
- snow:        chance = 0.05
- snowstorm:   chance = 0.0125
- thunder:     chance = 0.8 (restored to original — this controls how quickly
                thunder starts once heavy_rain is active, not spawn frequency)

-- Shelter-aware sound attenuation --

- utils.lua: Extended with shelter detection system (get_shelter_factor),
  shelter-aware sound management (update_weather_sound, clear_sound_state),
  per-weather gain profiles with outdoor/indoor/cave anchor points, and
  dynamic sound fading via minetest.sound_fade.

- weathers/light_rain.lua, rain.lua, heavy_rain.lua, snowstorm.lua,
  thunder.lua: Modified to integrate shelter-aware sound attenuation,
  corrected gain levels, and improved sound lifecycle management.

-- New weather types --

- weathers/light_fog.lua, moderate_fog.lua, heavy_fog.lua: New weather
  types adding three densities of fog with sky overlay, biome awareness,
  and shelter-aware particle rendering.

- weathers/pds_severe_thunderstorm.lua: New weather type implementing a
  five-phase "Particularly Dangerous Situation" severe thunderstorm with
  progressive sky darkening, ominous green sky hue, rain buildup, dynamic
  day/night ratio override, a low rumble sound during onslaught, escalating
  lightning frequency, and proportional wind-down. The full-intensity tier
  of severe weather (rare).

- weathers/severe_thunderstorm.lua: New weather type implementing a
  five-phase severe thunderstorm — a less intense counterpart to
  pds_severe_thunderstorm with no green sky hue, no rumble sound, reduced
  sky/cloud darkness, reduced lightning frequency during onslaught, and
  shorter phase durations. The moderate-intensity, more common tier of
  severe weather.

-- New assets --

- textures/weather_pack_fog.png: Original texture by TechnoWolfTV,
  released under MIT License, used for fog particle rendering.

- sounds/severe-storm-rumble.ogg: Used during pds_severe_thunderstorm
  onslaught phase only. "Low Rumbling | low-rumbling-176033.mp3"
  by Musheran (https://opengameart.org/content/low-rumbling)
  License: CC BY (http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/)

-- Other --

- commands.lua: Updated command descriptions to list all available weather
  codes inline, visible to players via /help in the Luanti client. Added
  /weather_status command showing active and disabled weathers. Added
  /stop_weather all to stop all active weathers at once. Added
  /disable_weather and /enable_weather commands (with 'all' support) to
  persistently enable or disable individual or all weather types across
  server restarts using mod storage. Intercepted happy_weather.request_to_start
  and happy_weather.register_weather to enforce disabled state globally.

- init.lua: Updated to load new weather modules.
